    },
    {
      "text": "While the old policy explained technical workarounds like preventing HTTP referrer leakage and avoiding POST requests, the new version simply states that device information like IP addresses and browser types are only used temporarily for delivery and security, and are never logged to disk alongside user activity. This simplifies the explanation while reinforcing that no persistent tracking occurs.",
